node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-77-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-78-A Server Action runs as a POST request against the page that invokes it. At build time, the `'use server'` directive tells the compiler to swap the function's implementation in client bundles for a reference (an action ID plus a dispatcher) that POSTs back to the server. The implementation stays on the server, but the route is reachable to anyone who can send the same POST. Treat every action as an untrusted entry point.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-79-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-80-Next.js enforces a few framework-level protections:
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-81-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-82-- **CSRF check.** The request's `Origin` is compared to the `Host` (or `X-Forwarded-Host`). Mismatches are rejected. Configure [`serverActions.allowedOrigins`](/docs/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/serverActions#allowedorigins) for proxy or CDN domains.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-83-- **Body size limit.** Action requests are capped at 1MB by default. Configure [`serverActions.bodySizeLimit`](/docs/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/serverActions#bodysizelimit) when accepting larger payloads.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md:84:- **Encrypted action IDs and dead code elimination.** Action references are encrypted at build time, and unused Server Functions are stripped from client bundles so they have no public endpoint. See [Built-in Server Actions security features](/docs/app/guides/data-security#built-in-server-actions-security-features).
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-85-- **Closure variable encryption.** Variables captured by an inline action are encrypted before being sent to the client. For multi-instance and self-hosted deployments, set `NEXT_SERVER_ACTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY` to a stable key shared across instances. See [Closures and encryption](/docs/app/guides/data-security#closures-and-encryption).
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-86-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-87-Framework protections are not a substitute for application-level checks. Inside every action:
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-88-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-89-- **Authenticate and authorize.** Render-time gating (only rendering a form on an authenticated page) is not a security boundary, because requests can be sent without going through the UI.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-90-- **Validate inputs.** Treat `FormData`, query parameters, and headers as untrusted.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-91-- **Constrain return values.** Action returns are serialized to the client. Shape them to what the UI renders, not raw database records.
