node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-174-Each Server Action is identified by the [action ID](#security) that is part of its build artifacts. New deployments typically generate new IDs (Next.js rotates them at most every 14 days, even when the source is unchanged), so a client still running the previous build may invoke an action ID that no longer exists. The error surfaces as "[Failed to find Server Action](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/failed-to-find-server-action)".
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-175-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-176-To minimize disruption:
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-177-
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-178-- Prefer rolling deployments over abrupt cutovers when active users are likely to be mid-mutation.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md-179-- Keep `NEXT_SERVER_ACTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY` stable across instances so action references remain decryptable everywhere.
node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/server-actions.md:180:- Surface the error as a retry path in the UI rather than a hard failure, so a refresh recovers the user.
